# Put the interfaces in their zones (this changes traffic at once):
#   zone FWS_untrust / interface ge-0/0/0.0
#   zone FWS_trust / interface ge-0/0/1.0
#   zone FWS_dmz / interface ge-0/0/2.0
#   zone FWS_dmz / interface ge-0/0/3.0
#   zone FWS_guest / interface ge-0/0/4.0
# Written inactive:
#   updates: host name object updates: the form of an address object of a host name is not in the documentation FWShift could read
#   guest-web: schedule 'work-hours' is not converted; the rule would apply at all times
#   guest-ping: references 'junos-ping': the predefined application junos-ping: Juniper describes it as ICMP echo, other readers of Junos as every ICMP type
#   global-ntp: service app-high: source ports, an ICMP code, SCTP ports or protocol 0, which a service object cannot say
